<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="chapter6" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Inverses</title>

  <introduction>

<p>
    In this chapter, we carefully analyze the concept of reversing a process and apply this analysis to processes associated with matrix multiplication.
</p>

<objectives>
    <title>Objectives for <xref ref="chp6sec1" /></title>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <p>I understand the concept reversing a process.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
            <p>I can use my understanding of matrix transformations to deduce the matrix of its inverse.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
            <p>I understand and can use the algebraic properties of inverses.</p>
        </li>
    </ul>
</objectives>

<objectives>
    <title>Objectives for <xref ref="chp6sec2" /></title>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <p>I can use the Inverse Algorithm to compute small inverses by hand.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
            <p>I can use the Inverse Algorithm to compute large inverses using GeoGebra.</p>
        </li>
    </ul>
</objectives>

  </introduction>

  <!-- include sections-->
    <xi:include href="chapter6sec1.ptx" />
    <xi:include href="chapter6sec2.ptx" />
   

</chapter>